            <ArticleTitle>Specific psychiatric morbidity among a sample of asthmatics in south western Nigeria.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>151-61</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="OBJECTIVE" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">This study was to identify specific psychiatric morbidity among asthma patients and to compare their rates to controls.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="METHOD" NlmCategory="METHODS">Hundred consecutive asthmatics were screened using the General Health Questionnaire (GHQ-30), and the Present State Examination (PSE). The same instruments were also administered to 75 healthy individuals, and 75 orthopaedic patients.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="RESULTS" NlmCategory="RESULTS">Patients with asthma had a higher occurrence of psychopathology. The specific psychiatric diagnoses among asthmatics were generalized anxiety disorder (23%), depressive disorder (11%), while 2% had panic disorder.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSION" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">Psychiatric morbidity is more common among asthmatics, than the general population and other patient group.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
